{"author":{"id":"86dc3c885e4fa466d19699d4a5e74c240f1c9d6b23f4e62ea2d2d8e359bd1711"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789490258,"nonce":"hNNfIFmHNMxzwSM5LJLDPozCyUI=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOUKdEis8AAAABRblxuA","github-url":"https://github.com/ff6347/giclang/issues/27","origin":"github"},"title":"Add native desktop document workflows","message":"## Parent\n\ngit-bug issue `60b2077` — PRD: GIC v0.9 workshop environment\n\n## What to build\n\nConnect the shared one-document model, examples, and recovery lifecycle to restricted native desktop file operations. Students receive native Open, Save, Save As, recent-file, rename, discard, and recovery behavior without broad filesystem access in the webview.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Native dialogs open and save one real `.gic` file with cancellation handled as a normal user action.\n- [ ] Save, Save As, format-on-save, dirty state, discard confirmation, and recent files follow the shared document contract.\n- [ ] Examples remain immutable sources and require Save As.\n- [ ] Recovery survives packaged restart without silently modifying the selected source file.\n- [ ] Renaming within GIC updates document identity; moved, missing, and deleted recent files have documented behavior.\n- [ ] Bridge contract tests use temporary real files and prove operations stay within paths explicitly selected or owned by the application.\n- [ ] Packaged macOS and Windows smoke tests cover file round-trips and restart recovery.\n\n## Blocked by\n\n- git-bug issue `5874fff` — Add the portable one-document workflow\n- git-bug issue `cab1222` — Add immutable examples and private recovery\n- git-bug issue `f264662` — Package the shared IDE in a desktop window","files":null}]}